{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734780",
      "title": "Adding Routes",
      "sourceHash": "a1f86267984980ea87cfcba6c732c928f188d9b904b38360b3f287042a7f1526",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "Now, which different paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 6.63,
          "en": "could we support in this demo website?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.63,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "Well, of course I still want have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 10.549,
          "en": "the starting page where I show all posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.549,
          "end": 13.5,
          "en": "but I then also wanna be able to get to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.5,
          "end": 14.85,
          "en": "this new post page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.85,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "so that should be a separate page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "Maybe still present it like this as a modal overlay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "but it should get its own path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 23.43,
          "en": "its own URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "And I also wanna be able to click on my posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 29.52,
          "en": "to load them in a modal on a detail page as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.52,
          "end": 33.69,
          "en": "so that I can also link to a single post if I want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.69,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "So I wanna have these three routes:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 37.62,
          "en": "starting page, new post page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.62,
          "end": 40.784,
          "en": "and post detail page if I click on a post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.784,
          "end": 43.38,
          "en": "And therefore we need to tell React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.38,
          "end": 46.421,
          "en": "and React Router that we wanna have these three posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.421,
          "end": 50.67,
          "en": "We can do so, for example in main JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.67,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "by first of all there importing something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 56.55,
          "en": "from react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "And the something we wanna import is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 62.493,
          "en": "the router provider component as it turns out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 65.55,
          "en": "And you should render that component instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 67.173,
          "en": "of the app component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 71.16,
          "en": "This enables Routing and tells React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.16,
          "end": 72.93,
          "en": "that it should watch the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 75.06,
          "en": "and start rendering different components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.06,
          "end": 76.73,
          "en": "for different paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.73,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "But just by adding it like this, it won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "And that hopefully makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "because of course you also must tell React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.39,
          "end": 87.12,
          "en": "which components should be loaded for which paths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.12,
          "end": 89.55,
          "en": "so you must configure the router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.55,
          "end": 92.7,
          "en": "That's why router provider takes a router prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 92.7,
          "end": 95.85300000000001,
          "en": "which wants a route configuration object as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 99.428,
          "en": "And that configuration object is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.428,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "with a function imported from react-router-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 105.543,
          "en": "which is called create browser router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "We can then call this function to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 111.42699999999999,
          "en": "such a route configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.42699999999999,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "and store that in a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "and pass that constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "that configuration object value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 121.203,
          "en": "as a value to the router prop on router provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "And now create browser router then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 126.033,
          "en": "takes an array as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.9,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "And this is simply an array of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "all the routes you wanna have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 132.123,
          "en": "a list of route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 136.173,
          "en": "And a route definition is simply an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 138.72,
          "en": "An object which typically should have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.72,
          "end": 141.39,
          "en": "a path property where you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "define the path of a single route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 145.77,
          "en": "So we could have multiple objects here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 145.77,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "and every object represents one route, one path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 152.599,
          "en": "and the component that should be loaded for the path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.599,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "So here we could have the path slash nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "as the main route, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "which then is loaded for our domain slash nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 165.24,
          "en": "which is equal to just entering our domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 165.24,
          "end": 167.07,
          "en": "So that's of course one important route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 167.07,
          "end": 168.498,
          "en": "we wanna support here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 168.498,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "and the path alone is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 173.64,
          "en": "Instead, you should also add the element property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 173.64,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "where you now define the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "that should be rendered on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 180.06,
          "en": "when this route becomes active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 183.21,
          "en": "so when this path is active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 186.03,
          "en": "And here in my case that is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 186.03,
          "end": 187.803,
          "en": "the app component for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 191.34,
          "en": "So the component which we previously rendered there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.34,
          "end": 193.35,
          "en": "is now the component that should be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 193.35,
          "end": 195.603,
          "en": "if the path is slash nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.78,
          "en": "With this simple change, if we save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.97,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "the app still works as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 206.04,
          "en": "because we load this app component for slash nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 206.04,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "So that's of course not too impressive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 211.556,
          "en": "But if I, for example, enter slash new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 211.556,
          "end": 213.42000000000002,
          "en": "I get an error instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 213.42000000000002,
          "end": 217.32,
          "en": "which already proves that something's going on here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "React Router is doing something because indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.623,
          "en": "it is telling me that it did not find this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "and that makes sense because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 228.66,
          "en": "I only defined this slash nothing route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 228.66,
          "end": 230.43,
          "en": "but that still works then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 230.43,
          "end": 232.74,
          "en": "But of course we don't just want to add one route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 232.74,
          "end": 234.48,
          "en": "we wouldn't gain much by that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "Instead we want to have multiple routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 237.87,
          "en": "and for example we wanted to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 237.87,
          "end": 240.573,
          "en": "a separate route for creating new posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 241.71,
          "end": 244.26,
          "en": "So how can we add this new post component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 244.26,
          "end": 245.94,
          "en": "as a separate route?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 245.94,
          "end": 249.24,
          "en": "Well, we can of course add a second route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 249.24,
          "end": 252.39,
          "en": "to this create browser router function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 256.44,
          "en": "and then maybe have a path of create dash post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 259.14,
          "en": "This path is of course totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 259.14,
          "end": 260.94,
          "en": "And then here we could say that we wanna",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 263.13,
          "en": "render an element and the element should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 263.13,
          "end": 265.204,
          "en": "the new post component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 265.204,
          "end": 268.41,
          "en": "For that you must import the new post component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 268.41,
          "end": 270.93,
          "en": "but then you can render it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 270.93,
          "end": 271.83,
          "en": "and you can by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 271.83,
          "end": 274.26,
          "en": "render any JSX code of your choice here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 274.26,
          "end": 276.63,
          "en": "could also be some h1 tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 276.63,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "But of course here in that case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 282.15,
          "en": "I wanna render the new post component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 284.944,
          "en": "Now if I do that and I then enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 284.944,
          "end": 287.763,
          "en": "create dash post here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 292.53,
          "en": "I indeed see this new post component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 292.53,
          "end": 293.94,
          "en": "not as a modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 293.94,
          "end": 295.8,
          "en": "and the rest of the app is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 295.8,
          "end": 298.2,
          "en": "And it also doesn't really work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 298.2,
          "end": 299.73,
          "en": "because upon submitting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 299.73,
          "end": 302.82,
          "en": "this prop value is not received anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 302.82,
          "end": 306.57,
          "en": "This value for on add post is not received anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 306.57,
          "end": 308.76,
          "en": "because I'm using this component now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 308.76,
          "end": 310.47,
          "en": "without setting any props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 310.47,
          "end": 313.98,
          "en": "but it technically, generally, still works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 313.98,
          "end": 316.839,
          "en": "At least I can see this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 316.839,
          "end": 320.16,
          "en": "But of course it's not rendered the way I'd like to see it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 320.16,
          "end": 321.81,
          "en": "Instead, it should still be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 321.81,
          "end": 324.39,
          "en": "as this overlay and this button should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "of course, still lead there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 328.53,
          "en": "And therefore we have to dive into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 328.53,
          "end": 331.26,
          "en": "another important feature offered by React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 331.26,
          "end": 334.443,
          "en": "and that's the feature of creating layout routes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}